<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yeondeunghoe</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lotus Lantern Festival</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yeondeunghoe is a Korean Buddhist lantern festival. In the Goryeo kingdom it was a state festival held early in the year, at which lanterns were lit in honour of the Buddha, alongside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palgwanhoe">Palgwanhoe</a>. It continues today as the lantern festival celebrating the Buddha's birthday and was inscribed on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a>'s list of intangible cultural heritage in 2020.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yeondeunghoe.jpg" alt="Yeondeunghoe" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 대한민국 정부 문화체육관광부 문화재청 · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EC%97%B0%EB%93%B1%ED%9A%8C.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
